# HR360 — AS-IS PROCESS MAPPING

**Document ID:** HR360-BA-003
**Version:** 1.0
**Status:** Draft for Review
**Date:** 20 September 2026
**Author:** Nida Khan

# 1. Purpose

This document describes the current-state HR operating model that HR360 is intended to improve.

The As-Is model provides the baseline for identifying process gaps and defining the future-state HR360 solution.

# 2. Current-State Overview

The current-state model represents HR information as distributed across multiple operational records and manually coordinated processes.

```text
HR / Business User
        ↓
Employee Information
        ↓
Separate Records
        ↓
Attendance Records
        ↓
Leave Records
        ↓
Performance Records
        ↓
Training Records
        ↓
Recruitment Records
        ↓
Manual Consolidation
        ↓
Management Reporting
```

# 3. Employee Management — As-Is

```text
Employee joins
      ↓
Employee details captured
      ↓
Department / Role assigned
      ↓
Information maintained in records
      ↓
Employee status manually reviewed
      ↓
HR reporting
```

# 4. Workforce Status — As-Is

```text
Employee information
        ↓
Department checked
        ↓
Employment / Work / Salary information checked
        ↓
Manual interpretation
        ↓
Active / Not Active classification
        ↓
Report
```

This creates a risk of inconsistent interpretation when different departments use different definitions.

# 5. Attendance and Leave — As-Is

```text
Attendance information
        ↓
Attendance record
        ↓
Separate leave information
        ↓
Manual consolidation
        ↓
Attendance / Leave report
```

# 6. Performance and Training — As-Is

```text
Performance information
        ↓
Performance review records
        ↓
PIP information where applicable
        ↓
Separate training records
        ↓
Manual consolidation
        ↓
Employee development reporting
```

# 7. Recruitment — As-Is

```text
Candidate
   ↓
Application
   ↓
Screening
   ↓
Interview
   ↓
Offer
   ↓
Hiring
```

Recruitment stages may require manual coordination between candidate information, application information, interviews and offers.

# 8. Management Reporting — As-Is

```text
Multiple HR Records
       ↓
Manual Data Collection
       ↓
Data Consolidation
       ↓
Manual KPI Calculation
       ↓
Management Report
```

# 9. Current-State Pain Points

| Area             | Current-State Challenge              |
| ---------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| Employee data    | Distributed information              |
| Workforce status | Manual interpretation                |
| Attendance       | Separate records                     |
| Leave            | Separate process                     |
| Performance      | Limited centralized visibility       |
| Training         | Separate tracking                    |
| Recruitment      | Multiple disconnected stages         |
| Reporting        | Manual consolidation                 |
| KPIs             | Potentially inconsistent definitions |

# 10. Business Analysis Conclusion

The As-Is analysis identifies the need for a centralized HR platform with common data structures, standardized business rules, integrated workflows and analytics capabilities.

The To-Be HR360 process will address these gaps through a centralized application and database.

**End of Document**
